+STATUS: PARTIAL
+Derived D51-U (unreviewed lane proof): for a full-H packet in `I=[c-w,c+w]`, `c<a_5`, the `>=5`-wall probability is uniformly bounded for all times.
+The bound uses `||QHP||<=3J/2` and `QHQ>=a_5Q`, `a_5=(5J/2)(Delta-1)`; on the Mq-E Fano band it is `O(Delta^-2)`.
+Derived the below-threshold Feshbach bounds `||Sigma||=O(J/Delta)` and `||partial_E Sigma||=O(Delta^-2)`.
+This does not prepare a full-H spectral packet, prove local decay, exclude other on-shell `<=3`-wall components, or prove D18/completeness.
+Exact next target: weighted projected LAP/Mourre estimate (D51-M) plus extra-channel exclusion or inventory.
+`d51_check.py` passes; `--red` fails as required.  Green/red outputs are saved.
+PATCH.md targets `claims/CLAIMS.md` and `theory/memory-quantization.md` by string anchors.
